#######
# Setup
#######

Context("LimitedNumeric");
$yesno=RadioButtons([
  "So -3 is a solution to this equation.",
  "So -3 is not a solution to this equation.",
  ], 1, showInStatic => 0
);

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
Is [`-3`] a solution to the equation [`2x-3=5-(4+x)\text{?}`]

>> [@DataTable(
  [
    [
     PGML('[`2x-3`]'),
     PGML('[`{}={}`]'),
     PGML('[`5-(4+x)`]'),
    ],
    [
     PGML('[_]{-9}{3}'),
     PGML('[`{}\wonder{=}{}`]'),
     PGML('[_]{4}{3}'),
    ],
  ],
      align => 'rcl',
      valign => 'middle',);@]* <<

[_]{$yesno}{5}

END_PGML

##########
# Solution
##########

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
We have to substitute [`-3`] in for [`x`] and simplify each side:

[```
\begin{aligned}
2x-3\amp=5-(4+x)\\
2(\substitute{-3})-3\amp\wonder{=}5-(4+(\substitute{-3}))\\
\highlight{-6}-3\amp\wonder{=} 5-(\highlight{1})\\
\highlight{-9}\amp\reject{=}\highlight{4}
\end{aligned}
```]

Since [`-9=4`] is false, [`-3`] is not a solution to this equation.

END_PGML_SOLUTION

#############
# End Problem
#############

ENDDOCUMENT();
